# dockerignore patterns are root-anchored, unlike .gitignore: '__pycache__/'
# alone matches only the context root's own dir. The nested '**/' forms are
# the load-bearing ones -- without them COPY benchmarks baked host-compiled
# pycs (Windows co_filename) into the worker image, and pytest's legacy junit
# file attribute followed them into every oracle task grade (D-B).
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
**/*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.env
env/
.venv/
.git/
.vscode/
.design/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
runs/
docs/superpowers/
